>n
You walk through the arch. It says nothing, with enormous tact, and Kess waves
you through without looking up.

Lift Lobby
A white hall with two lifts, one bright and one grey, side by side. A directory
on the wall lists SIXTY FLOORS, each in the same typeface. A service robot sits
in the corner, with its head against the wall. The security desk is back south.
A button says UP.

Ford ambles in after you, towel over one shoulder.

[The score has just gone up by eight points.]

>compliment cheerful lift
"Oh!" says the bright lift, quivering. "Oh, that's lovely. Nobody says that. I
think I'll go all the way up, just for you!" Its doors beam open. The grey lift
sighs, once, like a damp towel.

[The score has just gone up by ten points.]

>u
The lift glides up through the tower with a feeling of being politely
rearranged, and lets you out on the Editorial Floor.

The Editorial Floor
A huge open-plan floor of grey desks, each with a small plant that has been told
not to grow. A coffee machine mutters in a corner. A narrow stair at the north-
east corner runs up, guarded by a large, thoughtful Vogon. The boardroom is
north, an archive west, and a corner office east, its door ajar. A bright lift
hums to the south.

Zendra, who sits at the desk nearest the lift, looks up with something like
relief. 

Orlo stands at the foot of the north-east stairs, a notebook tucked under one
arm like a small, vulnerable animal. 

Ford ambles in after you, towel over one shoulder.

>ask zendra about mk ii
"It isn't right," says Zendra, lowering her voice. "The Mk II. It doesn't hold
entries. It holds readers. Every edit we make goes into it, and then it makes
its own: not about things, about people. I've seen it write a paragraph about a
man who hadn't arrived yet."

[The score has just gone up by three points.]

>ask zendra about infinidim
"Six names, one address," says Zendra. "The new management are very polite. They
use the word synergy as if they hope you won't ask. The editor-in-chief doesn't
have a name that anyone's been allowed to know."

[The score has just gone up by three points.]

>ask zendra about ford
"Ford," says Zendra, with a half-smile. "The only man to get a desk after being
sacked. His desk is at the end. He used to set the combination to the lengths of
the Earth entry, you know. Every draft. He was fond of it. It's all in the
archive."

[The score has just gone up by two points.]

>wear towel
You put on your old towel.

>n

The Boardroom
A long, pale room with a long, pale table and eleven chairs of exactly the same
pale. A vent in the ceiling hums. The editorial floor is south.

Ford ambles in after you, towel over one shoulder.

You stand against the wall with the towel over your head. The Vogons look
briefly at the place where you are, and then past it. This, you realise, is the
oldest trick there is, and also the worst, and it works.

>wait
Time passes.

"Item one," says the Chief Editor. "The variants. We have identified four
hundred and eleven. The Mk II reports that it has made contact with the
daughter. She is, apparently, very promising."

>wait
Time passes.

"Item two. The date. It is a Thursday, in London, on the Earth the girl has been
drawn to. Every other Earth is to be drawn to the same afternoon, in the same
room, by a method the Mk II describes as hospitality." A pause. "Item three. The
Grebulons."

>wait
Time passes.

"The Grebulons," says the Chief Editor, "have been engaged. They have a chart.
They have forgotten what it is for, which is useful. They will press the button
when the room is full." A rustle of agreement, like paper in a drawer.

>wait
Time passes.

"Adjourned," says the Chief Editor. The Vogons file out, in order of seniority,
and the room empties. You peel the towel off your head and breathe. Ford, beside
you with his own towel round his ears, looks at you with an expression you have
rarely seen on him: fear, and below it, determination.

[The score has just gone up by twelve points.]

