>w

The Archive
A long, silent room of grey steel stacks, a ladder on rails, and an overhead
light that clicks on when you enter and then waits to see what you'll do. There
is a locked cabinet drawer at the far end, and a faint smell of old ink. The
editorial floor is east.

Ford ambles in after you, towel over one shoulder.

>search stacks
You follow the arrow and find, between OUTDATED and OBSOLETE, a slim file marked
EARTH: REVISION HISTORY. Next to it is a heavy ledger labelled VOGON POETRY,
VOL. 9 (which nobody has ever wanted to borrow).

[The score has just gone up by four points.]

>read file
The file holds three drafts of one entry. DRAFT ONE, FORD: "Harmless." DRAFT
TWO, FORD: "Mostly harmless." DRAFT THREE, FORD, in the margin of a memo:
"Mostly harmless. Bring a towel." Each has been stamped REJECTED, then ACCEPTED,
then RE-ACCEPTED. The drafts, you notice, run to one word, two words and five.

>open ledger
You open the ledger, steeling yourself, and a small brass key slides out from
between the verses and clatters to the floor. Whoever hid it had judged
correctly that nobody would ever look here.

>take key
Taken.

>unlock drawer with key
You unlock the cabinet drawer.

>open drawer
You open the cabinet drawer, revealing an Infinidim memorandum.

[The score has just gone up by three points.]

>read memo
MEMORANDUM. FROM: INFINIDIM ENTERPRISES (ONE OF SIX). SUBJECT: CONSOLIDATION OF
EARTH VARIANTS. The management has identified four hundred and eleven variants
of the planet Earth, to be removed at a single stroke in the interest of
administrative simplicity. The Mk II will draw all variants together onto a
single afternoon, in a single room, on a single Earth. The Grebulon fleet has
been engaged to execute. The coordinates of the room are held in the Mk II core.
NOTE: THIS MEMORANDUM SHOULD NOT EXIST.

[The score has just gone up by five points.]

