Ford's Old Office
A cramped corner office with a window onto the plaza, still bearing the faint
signs of a man who used it to avoid working. Torn proofs hang on the wall; a
battered desk with a dial lock on its top drawer stands under the window. The
editorial floor is west.

Ford ambles in after you, towel over one shoulder.

>dial 1 2 5
The dials click. The top drawer slides open with a sigh of old tobacco and the
faint smell of other people's coffee. Inside are Ford's old pass, and a thin
folder of proofs.

